//Association

Association is a general relationship where two classes/objects are connected or interact with each other.

It does not necessarily mean ownership.

Example:

class Teacher {
public:
    void teach() {
        cout << "Teaching";
    }
};

class Student {
public:
    void learn(Teacher& t) {
        t.teach();
    }
};

Here:

Student interacts with Teacher
A Student does not own the Teacher
Both can exist independently
Student ←→ Teacher
      interaction
Composition vs Aggregation vs Association
Composition → strong has-a
Aggregation → weak has-a
Association → general relationship/interaction

Simple definition:

Association = a relationship where two independent classes/objects are connected or interact with each other.